# Generated identity ledger + its receipt, both written by
# tools/scripts/gpu_handoff_provenance.py. The receipt is what collides
# unconditionally: source_commit and the handoff_sha256 over the whole ledger
# move on every regeneration, whatever else did. The ledger itself is milder —
# a row is pinned to the commit that last touched its own path, so a main move
# re-pins only the rows whose paths it touched — and it is a hybrid rather than
# a generated file, because the inventory of rows is a human edit. The driver
# resolves what it can to a deliberately invalid value that gates.sh rejects,
# turning a hand-resolved conflict into one mechanical regeneration. Install it
# with setup.sh (or tools/scripts/install-githooks.sh); a checkout without it
# gets today's text conflict, which is the status quo rather than a worse
# outcome. Feature branches should not be regenerating these at all —
# gpu_handoff_pin_freshness.py rejects an identity-only refresh at push.
docs/status/gpu-vellum-handoff.yaml merge=pulp-gpu-ledger
docs/validation/gpu-handoff-provenance/receipt.json merge=pulp-gpu-ledger
